  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "With a live-shaped `/work` response (fixture above), `MyWork` renders without throwing and shows the existing error card \u2014 verify: new vitest case in `frontend/tests/my-work.test.tsx` asserts `role=\"alert\"` with \"We couldn't load your queue\" and no thrown error; `cd frontend && npx vitest run tests/my-work.test.tsx`.",
    "The same guard covers refresh and Show more: a live-shaped row on either path does not throw, and rows already shown stay \u2014 verify: two further vitest cases in the same file.",
    "The v7 mock behaviour is unchanged \u2014 verify: the existing `my-work.test.tsx`, `my-work-model.test.ts` and `e2e/my-work.spec.ts` pass unedited. `git diff` shows no change to existing assertions.",
    "No new design and no new words \u2014 verify: `git diff` over `frontend/src` adds no new user-visible string, no CSS change and no new component. The error card text matches the existing copy at `MyWork.tsx` (about line 352).",
    "Live check \u2014 verify: against the local backend on 55433 as `qa-seed`, with lane C's work item 1 (a weekly report) present, open `/my-work`. The page shows the error card, the console has no uncaught error, and the shell stays up. Attach a screenshot of the state shown to the round evidence.",
    "Negative: a v7 row with a valid `kind` among live-shaped ones still fails the whole response and shows the error card \u2014 verify: vitest case with a mixed list."
  ],
